Question:

“When would you use a heap instead of sorting?”

Strong answer structure:

> “If I repeatedly need the minimum or maximum, or only need the top K elements, a heap can be more efficient than sorting the entire dataset. For example, finding the K largest elements can be done using a heap of size K in O(n log K) time.”



